CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ non-template member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The explicit instantiation declaration instantiates str<char> before its
members' definitions.  The out-of-class definition of the member template
find was then given to every same-named member of matching arity without
a body, the non-template find(char, size_type) included.  libc++'s
std::string::find(char) returned what the string_view overload's
body computed.
